<title>HONG KONG: Hongkong Bank sets HK$150 mln fungible CD.</title>
<headline>Hongkong Bank sets HK$150 mln fungible CD.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hongkong and Shanghai Banking Corp has lodged a HK$150 million fixed rate certificates of deposit issue with the Hong Kong Monetary Authority Central Moneymarkets Unit.</p>
<p>The 7.87 percent certificates due November 10, 2003, were issued at par. HSBC Markets was the arranger.</p>
<p>The new issue will be fungible with a previous issue of HK$50 million fixed rate CDs due November 2003.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6960</p>
</text>
